language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Mr Greenguest chooses which green items to wear (tie t, hat h, shirt r, socks s) and whether to pay the entrance fee n, at minimum total cost.
find t : bool
find h : bool
find r : bool
find s : bool
find n : bool

$ cost: green tie $10, green hat $2, green socks $12, entrance fee $11; the green shirt is owned, so it costs nothing
minimising 10 * t + 2 * h + 12 * s + 11 * n
such that
$ rule 1: if someone wears a green tie he has to wear a green shirt
t -> r,
$ rule 2: a guest may only wear green socks and a green shirt if he wears a green tie or a green hat
(s /\ r) -> (t \/ h),
$ rule 3: a guest wearing a green shirt or a green hat or who does not wear green socks must wear a green tie
(r \/ h \/ !s) -> t,
$ rule 4: a guest who is not dressed according to rules 1-3 must pay the entrance fee
(n \/ ((t -> r) /\ ((s /\ r) -> (t \/ h)) /\ ((r \/ h \/ !s) -> t)))
